    "vernacular": "Lakeside port city at about 774 m on Lake Tanganyika with a hot tropical-savanna climate. The centre keeps Belgian-era (1920s-60s) low-rise modernist and colonial blocks: 1-3 storey painted-render buildings, shop arcades, flat concrete roofs and red or grey corrugated-iron roofs. Residential districts are single-storey houses of render or brick behind walls, with red earth streets, mango, palm and flamboyant trees, and lakeshore bars and beach clubs.",
